123:| **SquadAttack(objective, threat)** | assessment says suppression is achievable; a covered and concealed route exists for the manoeuvre element to an assault position at least 45-55 degrees from the base of fire and within 40 m of the objective (planner exposure below threshold from known threats); strength ratio acceptable under template and profile | Prepare: base of fire established. Move: manoeuvre element bounds along the covered route by buddy rushes of at most 5 s between covers; pause if base-of-fire evidence is lost for more than 8 s; entry into any stage within 18 m of the objective or of a known threat is gated on that threat being covered. Assault: line at 5 m intervals; lift or shift signal sent before crossing the base-of-fire lane; assault through the objective by fire and movement. Consolidate: occupy positions oriented on remaining known threats; base of fire moves up. Reorganise | complete when at least half of the manoeuvre element occupies the objective area with receipts and no known live enemy remains inside its radius; one alternate route allowed when a fresh threat exposes the corridor, then `Blocked`; fail on `InsufficientStrength` or support lost beyond timeout |
125:| **Occupy(area, sectors)** | platoon task or consolidation | positions with mutual support and sectors; elements keep separation | ends only by supersession; reports observed contacts |
126:| **Observe(area)** | platoon task or assessment needs information | cognition's observation semantics retained: a viewpoint with a line inside sight range; a fresh sighting or clearance completes; silence times out with an explicit nothing-learned report | as cognition |
132:Goals in priority order, each preemptible with receipts: Survive (effective suppression above the existing threshold, shelter within reach chosen with occupancy) > FollowOrder (current assignment) > EngageKnownThreat (fire from cover at known contacts in sector) > KeepFormationSlot (adjust when drift exceeds 1.5 intervals) > Scan. Tasks map onto the existing `Task` and `Completion` pairs initially (transit, occupy with slot, overwatch, rifle support, hold, observe, pull back); `Suppress` reuses the bounded area-fire behaviour proven in reliability fixture 27, and `Rush` is a short bound with at most 5 s of exposure. New enum values are appended only when a mapping does not exist.
136:`Sim/PlatoonTaskSim` builds a declarative task tree from the commander's own knowledge. Tasks: Advance(sector) by default, Fix(known enemy group), Flank(objective, side), Secure(sector), Reserve, Merge(squad into squad), Withdraw. Each task carries priority, capacity in squads, an area of operation, an activation condition on the commander's knowledge, a filter (for example needs a support weapon) and status. Squads flow to the highest-priority unfilled task by greedy assignment minimising `H(squad, task)` = travel time along the planner + coordination penalties (a fixing squad without potential lines, a flank without a fix) + tree balance + profile bias - a stickiness credit for the current assignment. Reallocation happens on activation and deactivation events and otherwise at the existing 5 s cadence. Directives expire after 60-90 s with renewal, never the whole battle.
138:Envelopment procedure on contact: group known contacts (minimum spanning tree, 20 m threshold); flanks are the extreme contacts relative to the platoon centroid; candidate flank objectives lie 30-40 m beyond each flank and require a covered route (planner exposure below threshold); the better side wins by route quality; the fixing squad is the one that can reach positions with lines to the group within its weapon range; by default 60 % of available squads flank inside their own corridors and the remainder holds in reserve in its own area behind the fixing element. Corridor claims add cost to other squads' routes. When no covered route exists: Fix plus Observe plus Reserve, and an honest report upward. Withdraw when believed strength ratio falls below one half with no support. Lift and shift: the fixing element receives the assault element's phase-line receipt through command transport and uses the existing fire-lane messages. Leader death degrades to squad-autonomous drills under the template's succession rule.
144:- Spatial: nearest-squadmate distance median and share under 2 m; squad radius; minimum inter-squad centroid distance; area-of-operation compliance.
145:- Tactical conformance: share of moving-soldier seconds covered by friendly delivered fire on the relevant known threat area in the preceding 6 s; assault arrival angle relative to the base of fire; exposed seconds without a firing solution; suppression established before assault; break contact when outnumbered; friendly-fire hits; gun-silent seconds after a gunner casualty.

